// The café's till poll – a sibling of cafe.json5 for two limits of the fixed fit cutoffs that the café's
// own survey, which fits its generating model, cannot show. Used by the "Does the model fit?" section of
// docs/en/concepts/latent-variables.md. A tablet at the till asked 300 visitors twelve quick questions.
// Generated by the exam builder's authored spec format (docs/en/exam-spec-reference.md):
//
//   app-gen --spec docs/examples/cafe-poll.json5 --name cafe-poll --authored
//
// The name is the seed, so `--name cafe-poll` reproduces the dataset exactly; cafe-poll.csv is that
// dataset, written as cafe.csv is. Every number the concept page quotes from it comes from that file,
// so a change to anything here – the name included – is a change to the prose.
// cafe-poll.ru.csv is this dataset with its header translated (места, свет, музыка, столы, пол, чашки,
// один, книга, добавка, десерт, ноутбук, телефон), every value identical.
//
// Structure, two item sets with two lessons:
//   - six three-point items (1 = no, 2 = partly, 3 = yes) on the room: "Were the seats comfortable?",
//     "Was the lighting pleasant?", "Was the music pleasant?" (Comfort) and "Were the tables clean?",
//     "Was the floor clean?", "Were the cups clean?" (Tidiness). Two factors correlated 0.6, which the
//     page fits as one on purpose: the same misspecified model under ML and under WLSMV, so the reader
//     sees one misfit read differently by two estimators
//   - six 1–5 items on how often the visitor comes alone, reads a book, orders a refill, has dessert,
//     works on a laptop, uses their phone. One weak factor (Lingering, loadings 0.30–0.40), plus a second
//     (Work) that laptop and phone share – in a one-factor CFA, a residual covariance between the two.
//     The correlations are 0.02–0.27, so the baseline model's RMSEA falls below 0.158 and even the
//     generating model reads a CFI below 0.95
// No missing data and no deliberate flaws.
{
	n: 300,
	factors: ["Comfort", "Tidiness", "Lingering", "Work"],
	phi: { "Comfort~Tidiness": 0.6 },
	// The room items: three answers, the middle one the most common
	defaults: { family: "ordinal", params: [-0.6, 0.6] },
	variables: {
		seats: { load: "Comfort*0.75" },
		light: { load: "Comfort*0.70" },
		music: { load: "Comfort*0.65" },
		tables: { load: "Tidiness*0.75" },
		floor: { load: "Tidiness*0.70" },
		cups: { load: "Tidiness*0.65" },
		// The visit items: 1 = never … 5 = always
		alone: { load: "Lingering*0.40", params: [-1.6, -0.8, 0.0, 0.9] },
		book: { load: "Lingering*0.35", params: [-1.6, -0.8, 0.0, 0.9] },
		refill: { load: "Lingering*0.35", params: [-1.6, -0.8, 0.0, 0.9] },
		dessert: { load: "Lingering*0.30", params: [-1.6, -0.8, 0.0, 0.9] },
		laptop: { load: "Lingering*0.35 + Work*0.45", params: [-1.6, -0.8, 0.0, 0.9] },
		phone: { load: "Lingering*0.35 + Work*0.45", params: [-1.6, -0.8, 0.0, 0.9] },
	},
}
